  "FIFO (in order per group)": "FIFO（同一組依序）",
  "FIFO (like SQS FIFO or a Kafka partition): messages of one group (one key) are handed out one at a time; the next one goes only when the previous one is done, dropped or moved to the DLQ. When one is stuck (slow, or a poison message retried again and again), its whole group waits (head-of-line blocking).": "FIFO（像 SQS FIFO、Kafka 的 partition）：同一組（同一個 key）的訊息一次只交出一則，前一則做完、失敗丟掉或進 DLQ 才交下一則。前一則卡住（處理很慢、毒訊息一直重試），後面整組都等（head-of-line blocking）。",
  "FIFO and head-of-line blocking": "FIFO 和隊頭阻塞",
  "FIFO {id}: {n} messages waited behind an earlier message of their group": "FIFO {id}：{n} 則訊息排在同組前一則後面等",
  "FIFO: messages that waited because an earlier one of their group was not done (head-of-line blocking)": "FIFO：同一組前一則還沒做完，這則只能等（head-of-line blocking）",
